                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any salt or ester of glutamic acid."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bb99448f-4789-33ee-84e6-1f305bdfd407",
                                        "entry_id": "e7015215-241e-35c6-b13d-e6eea2ec6edb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The anion of glutamic acid in its role as a neurotransmitter."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9c755b1a-8a4d-4ad0-890d-5c067bb0860c",
                                                "sense_id": "bb99448f-4789-33ee-84e6-1f305bdfd407",
                                                "text": "At a synaptic level, the axon terminal having to repeatedly release glutamate is the lecturer droning on repetitively; the moment when the postsynaptic threshold is passed and the NMDA receptors first activate is the dendritic spine finally getting it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0f26a7e3-641f-4812-9d49-1030720b8968",
                        "source_entry_id": "1ad7fd35-8e9e-35fb-a57c-788b40ef1e81",
                        "source_sense_id": "05160fba-66ff-3cd6-a1ab-dfd2c85274e6",
